/-
# Generators of groups generated by subgroups of coprime orders (Kourovka Notebook Problem 16.53)

Kourovka Notebook, Problem 16.53 (A. Lucchini): let `d(G)` denote the smallest cardinality of a
generating set of `G`. Suppose that `G = ⟨A, B⟩`, where `A` and `B` are two `d`-generated finite
groups of coprime orders. Is it true that `d(G) ≤ d + 1`?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Lattice
public import Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.CoprimeGenerationRankKourovka16Problem53Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 16.53 (A. Lucchini). UnsolvedMath record
UM-00701245 (`KOU-16.53`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`A` and `B` are subgroups of a finite group `G` with `A ⊔ B = ⊤`; `d`-generated means generated by a
family `Fin d → A` (repetitions allowed, so at most `d` elements), and `d(G) ≤ d + 1` means that `G`
is generated by a family `Fin (d + 1) → G`.
-/

/-- Kourovka 16.53 (A. Lucchini): if a finite group `G` is generated by subgroups `A` and `B` of
coprime orders, each generated by `d` elements, then `G` is generated by `d + 1` elements. -/
def coprimeGeneratedRankBound : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (A B : Subgroup G) (d : ℕ),
    Nat.Coprime (Nat.card A) (Nat.card B) → A ⊔ B = ⊤ →
    (∃ a : Fin d → A, Subgroup.closure (Set.range a) = ⊤) →
    (∃ b : Fin d → B, Subgroup.closure (Set.range b) = ⊤) →
    ∃ g : Fin (d + 1) → G, Subgroup.closure (Set.range g) = ⊤

/--
Resolved false: Muliarchyk (Theorem 1) constructs, for every `d ≥ 2`, a finite group `G = ⟨A, B⟩`
with `|A|` and `|B|` coprime, `d(A) = d(B) = d` and `d(G) = d + 2` (`A` and `B` metabelian of
exponents 6 and 55, inside a finite power of `PSL₂(11)`); the Kourovka Notebook (21st issue) answers
16.53 "No, not always". Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group
Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 16.53 (A. Lucchini);
resolution: K. Muliarchyk, Coprime generation through coset counts: a counterexample to Kourovka
Notebook Problem 16.53, preprint (2026), Theorem 1 (for every d ≥ 2 finite groups A_d, B_d ≤ G_d =
⟨A_d, B_d⟩ with coprime orders, d(A_d) = d(B_d) = d and d(G_d) = d + 2); the Kourovka Notebook (21st
issue) marks 16.53 solved (No, not always),
https://kourovkanotebookorg.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kourovka_16_53_solution.pdf.
-/
public theorem_wanted coprimeGeneratedRankBound_refuted : ¬ coprimeGeneratedRankBound

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.CoprimeGenerationRankKourovka16Problem53Wanted
